('','webform.webform.quiz_ash2','a:21:{s:4:\"uuid\";s:36:\"4349d162-29ad-443d-a97b-a7e75d4f20f7\";s:8:\"langcode\";s:2:\"en\";s:6:\"status\";s:4:\"open\";s:12:\"dependencies\";a:1:{s:6:\"module\";a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"vaxia_core\";}}s:6:\"weight\";i:0;s:4:\"open\";N;s:5:\"close\";N;s:3:\"uid\";i:0;s:8:\"template\";b:0;s:7:\"archive\";b:0;s:2:\"id\";s:9:\"quiz_ash2\";s:5:\"title\";s:19:\"ASH Test 2 - Ruling\";s:11:\"description\";N;s:10:\"categories\";a:0:{}s:8:\"elements\";s:19842:\"question_1:\n  \'#title\': \'Case 1 - Difficulty\'\n  \'#description\': \"<strong>Case 1 - Single-Trait Ruling</strong><br>\\n<em>Your Narrative:</em> \\\"In the newly fallen snow, the night air seems crisp. You four have been called to help capture the dreaded wendigo that has been terrorizing these woods for weeks.  You reach the forest’s edge, and all seems still except for the distant, sporadic cracking of the ice-laden branches of trees.<br>\\n<br>\\nActions?\\\"<br>\\n<br>\\n<em>Player 1 (Daedlus):</em> \\\"Daedlus scours the earth like a nearsighted hawk. This hunt is no simple trip, he feels something momentus will occur, some magical feeling within him that says \\\"this isn\'t your everyday wendigo hunt.\\\" He watches, peering into the dark with his elven eyes, and waiting for some sign of something large, white and furry.\\\"<br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>(1d100) + awa (25) + Forest Scouting (35) =&gt; Might: 60, Roll: 37</strong><br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Question 1</strong> - What difficulty would you set for the Awareness check?\"\n  \'#description_display\': before\n  \'#type\': radios\n  \'#options\':\n    a1: \'5\'\n    a2: \'25\'\n    a3: \'50\'\n    a4: \'70\'\n  \'#required\': true\nquestion_2:\n  \'#title\': \'Case 1 - Points Produced\'\n  \'#description\': \"<strong>Case 1 - Single-Trait Ruling</strong><br>\\n<em>Your Narrative:</em> \\\"In the newly fallen snow, the night air seems crisp. You four have been called to help capture the dreaded wendigo that has been terrorizing these woods for weeks.  You reach the forest’s edge, and all seems still except for the distant, sporadic cracking of the ice-laden branches of trees.<br>\\n<br>\\nActions?\\\"<br>\\n<br>\\n<em>Player 1 (Daedlus):</em> \\\"Daedlus scours the earth like a nearsighted hawk. This hunt is no simple trip, he feels something momentus will occur, some magical feeling within him that says \\\"this isn\'t your everyday wendigo hunt.\\\" He watches, peering into the dark with his elven eyes, and waiting for some sign of something large, white and furry.\\\"<br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>(1d100) + awa (25) + Forest Scouting (35) =&gt; Might: 60, Roll: 37</strong><br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Question 2</strong> - About how many points were produced on Daedlus\' roll? (Assume the AWA skill applies in this situation)\"\n  \'#description_display\': before\n  \'#type\': radios\n  \'#options\':\n    a1: 3-7\n    a2: 11-15\n    a3: 19-21\n    a4: \'None, he failed\'\n  \'#required\': true\nquestion_3:\n  \'#title\': \'Case 1 - Narrative\'\n  \'#description\': \"<strong>Case 1 - Single-Trait Ruling</strong><br>\\n<em>Your Narrative:</em> \\\"In the newly fallen snow, the night air seems crisp. You four have been called to help capture the dreaded wendigo that has been terrorizing these woods for weeks.  You reach the forest’s edge, and all seems still except for the distant, sporadic cracking of the ice-laden branches of trees.<br>\\n<br>\\nActions?\\\"<br>\\n<br>\\n<em>Player 1 (Daedlus):</em> \\\"Daedlus scours the earth like a nearsighted hawk. This hunt is no simple trip, he feels something momentus will occur, some magical feeling within him that says \\\"this isn\'t your everyday wendigo hunt.\\\" He watches, peering into the dark with his elven eyes, and waiting for some sign of something large, white and furry.\\\"<br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>(1d100) + awa (25) + Forest Scouting (35) =&gt; Might: 60, Roll: 37</strong><br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Question 3</strong> - Of the following narratives, pick the one which best describes the result based on those points produced.\"\n  \'#description_display\': before\n  \'#type\': radios\n  \'#options\':\n    a1: \'Daedlus catches sight of a white blur about a hundred yards away, large enough to be the monster they’re seeking.  It seems to be moving away from them in a hurry.\'\n    a2: \'Daedlus hears something at a distance, off to the north.\'\n    a3: \'A branch cracks above Daedlus’ head, distracting him\'\n    a4: \'Daedlus sees the wendigo looking at them half a mile away through the thick underbrush, its mouth moving in the gesture of words that may be the start of a teleportation spell.\'\n  \'#options_randomize\': true\n  \'#required\': true\nquestion_4:\n  \'#title\': \"Case 2 - Magic\\nMorpheus is a shapeshifting mage...\"\n  \'#description\': \"<strong>Case 2 - Magic</strong><br>\\nMorpheus is a shapeshifting mage, and would like to turn himself into a cheetah briefly to shorten his journey across town.  <br>\\n<br>\\nHis mights are as follows:  INT 50, SPI 45, Transformation 45.  <br>\\n<br>\\nHe rolls 23 on the INT roll, and 12 on the SPI roll.  <br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Question 1</strong> - Does he succeed in turning himself into a cheetah?  If so, roughly how many points did he produce?\"\n  \'#description_display\': before\n  \'#type\': radios\n  \'#options\':\n    a1: \'No, he failed\'\n    a2: \'Yes, he succeeded with roughly 8 points produced\'\n    a3: \'Yes, he succeeded with roughly 15 points produced\'\n    a4: \'Yes, he succeeded with roughly 3 points produced\'\n  \'#options_randomize\': true\n  \'#required\': true\nquestion_5:\n  \'#title\': \"Case 2 - Magic\\nMorpheus is a shapeshifting mage...\"\n  \'#description\': \"<strong>Case 2 - Magic</strong><br>\\nMorpheus is a shapeshifting mage, and would like to turn himself into a cheetah briefly to shorten his journey across town.   <br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Question 2</strong> - Assuming he did fail, with a failsby of 27, how would you describe the result?\"\n  \'#description_display\': before\n  \'#type\': radios\n  \'#options\':\n    a1: \'\"Morpheus failed to turn into a cheetah, but nothing happens.\"\'\n    a2: \'\"As Morpheus tries to shift into cheetah form, something goes awry, and he feels his leg bones warp incorrectly, leaving him in great pain.  He will need to try to shift again before he’ll be able to walk anywhere to get help.\"\'\n    a3: \'\"Morpheus\'\' insides rearrange themselves into the wrong places when he attempts the change.  With his heart where his hand should be, he goes into system shock, and dies.\"\'\n    a4: \'\"Morpheus manages to change only his legs, walking about with spots and claws, but otherwise looking perfectly human.\"\'\n  \'#options_randomize\': true\n  \'#required\': true\nquestion_6:\n  \'#title\': \'Case 2 - Diff vs PP\'\n  \'#description\': \"<strong>Case 2 - Magic</strong><br>\\nMorpheus is a shapeshifting mage, and would like to turn himself into a cheetah briefly to shorten his journey across town.  <br>\\n<br>\\nHis mights are as follows:  INT 50, SPI 45, Transformation 45.  <br>\\n<br>\\nHe rolls 23 on the INT roll, and 12 on the SPI roll.  <br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Question 3</strong> - Morpheus wants to go for a longer-lasting change.  Which of the following would you raise to signify the longer duration?\"\n  \'#description_display\': before\n  \'#type\': radios\n  \'#options\':\n    a1: Difficulty\n    a2: \'Points Produced\'\n    a3: Both\n  \'#required\': true\nquestion_7:\n  \'#title\': \'Case 3 - Area Magic\'\n  \'#description\': \"<strong>Case 3 - Multiple Targets</strong><br>\\n<br>\\nJasmine the fire mage wants to blast the three bandits in front of her with a single wave of fiery force.<br>\\n<br>\\nHow would you handle the rolls, difficulties and damage?\"\n  \'#description_display\': before\n  \'#type\': radios\n  \'#options\':\n    a1: \"Apply a +40 difficulty to her actions, and rule each one individually versus each target\'s defensive mights\"\n    a2: \"Have Jasmine roll once using the highest defender\'s mights as her difficulty, and deal that much PP to each target\"\n    a3: \'Have Jasmine roll against the base difficulty for the spell (25), then have each defender roll their defense, and subtract their PP from hers.  The remainder is divided evenly among the targets.\'\n  \'#options_randomize\': true\n  \'#required\': true\nquestion_8:\n  \'#title\': \"Case 3 - Multiple Targets\\n\\nJasmine the fire mag...\"\n  \'#description\': \"<strong>Case 3 - Multiple Targets</strong><br>\\n<br>\\nJasmine the fire mage wants to blast the three bandits in front of her with a single wave of fiery force.<br>\\n<br>\\nLet\'s say she has INT 50, SPI 50, and Pyromancy at 45.<br>\\n<br>\\nShe rolls a 1 for INT and a 79 for SPI in her attempt to make the wave of fire.<br>\\n<br>\\nThe bandits she\'s targeting have DEX 25 and END 25.<br>\\n<br>\\nHow would you describe the result?\"\n  \'#description_display\': before\n  \'#type\': radios\n  \'#options\':\n    a1: \"Jasmine\'s fiery blast has power but no control.  It goes sideways, blasting her friend instead of the bandits.\"\n    a2: \"Sending a waves of flame whipping about, Jasmine narrowly misses the bandits, who dodge out of the way of the frantic spell.  Instead, the flames set the bandits\' tents on fire, causing their bedrolls to go up in smoke.\"\n    a3: \'Jasmine succeeds in casting a wave of fire at the three bandits.\'\n    a4: \'Jasmine fails to cast the spell\'\n  \'#options_randomize\': true\n  \'#required\': true\nquestion_9:\n  \'#title\': \"Case 4 - Combat\\nPhylus the nimble half-elf has ...\"\n  \'#description\': \"<strong>Case 4 - Combat</strong><br>\\nPhylus the nimble half-elf has run sour of a dwarf named Furbeard in a local bar.  Combat ensues.  Phylus has LIF 40, the dwarves both have LIF 25.  <br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Round 1! </strong> <br>\\nStill hoping for a peaceful resolution, Phylus raises his shield to try to block Furbeard’s attack.  The dwarf, meanwhile, has grabbed his tankard as a dangerous weapon and seems intent on bashing Phylus’ head in for the offense.<br>\\n<br>\\nPhylus rolls: <br>\\n(1d100) + dex (35) + Sword and Shield (40) + Wooden Shield (-1) =&gt; Might: 74, Roll: 19<br>\\n(1d100) + str (40) + Sword and Shield (40) + Longsword (Medium) =&gt; Might: 80, Roll: 50<br>\\n(1d100) + end (30) + Sword and Shield (40) + Wooden Shield (5) =&gt; Might: 75, Roll: 37<br>\\n<br>\\nFurbeard rolls:<br>\\n(1d100) + dex (30) + Bar Combat (35) =&gt; Might: 65, Roll: 58<br>\\n(1d100) + str (50) + Bar Combat (35) + Metal Tankard (Light) =&gt; Might: 85, Roll: 53<br>\\n(1d100) + end (40) + Bar Combat (35) =&gt; Might: 75, Roll: 21<br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Question 1</strong> - Did Phylus take damage this round?  If so, how much?\"\n  \'#description_display\': before\n  \'#type\': radios\n  \'#options\':\n    a1: \'No, he took no damage\'\n    a2: \'Yes, he took 4-5 damage\'\n    a3: \'Yes, he took 9-10 damage\'\n    a4: \'Yes, he took 14-15 damage\'\n  \'#options_randomize\': true\n  \'#required\': true\nquestion_10:\n  \'#title\': \"Case 4 - Combat\\nPhylus the nimble half-elf has ...\"\n  \'#description\': \"<strong>Case 4 - Combat</strong><br>\\nPhylus the nimble half-elf has run sour of a dwarf named Furbeard in a local bar.  Combat ensues.  Phylus has LIF 40, the dwarves both have LIF 25.  <br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Round 2!</strong>  <br>\\nFurbeard’s loyal (and very drunk) friend, Chief Burlap, rushes in to assist Furbeard in taking Phylus down.  Both dwarves attack.  Phylus tries to block the newcomer, Burlap, and then attack Furbeard to discourage the other dwarf from continuing this fight.<br>\\n<br>\\nPhylus rolls: <br>\\n(2d100) + dex (35) + Sword and Shield (40) + Wooden Shield (-1) =&gt; Might: 74, Roll: 23, 92<br>\\n(2d100) + str (40) + Sword and Shield (40) + Longsword (Medium) =&gt; Might: 80, Roll: 41, 99<br>\\n(2d100) + end (30) + Sword and Shield (40) + Wooden Shield (5) =&gt; Might: 75, Roll: 84, 2<br>\\n<br>\\nFurbeard rolls:<br>\\n(1d100) + dex (30) + Bar Combat (35) =&gt; Might: 65, Roll: 45<br>\\n(1d100) + str (50) + Bar Combat (35) + Metal Tankard (Light) =&gt; Might: 85, Roll: 43<br>\\n(1d100) + end (40) + Bar Combat (35) =&gt; Might: 75, Roll: 72<br>\\n<br>\\nChief Burlap rolls:<br>\\n(1d100) + dex (20) + Bar Combat (40) =&gt; Might: 60, Roll: 32<br>\\n(1d100) + str (60) + Bar Combat (40) + Pointy Tankard (Light) =&gt; Might: 100, Roll: 47<br>\\n(1d100) + end (30) + Bar Combat (40) =&gt; Might: 70, Roll: 17<br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Question 2</strong> - How much total damage does Phylus take this round?\"\n  \'#description_display\': before\n  \'#type\': radios\n  \'#options\':\n    a1: 14-15\n    a2: 26-27\n    a3: 9-10\n    a4: 5-6\n  \'#options_randomize\': true\n  \'#required\': true\nquestion_11:\n  \'#title\': \"Case 4 - Combat\\nPhylus the nimble half-elf has ...\"\n  \'#description\': \"<strong>Case 4 - Combat</strong><br>\\nPhylus the nimble half-elf has run sour of a dwarf named Furbeard in a local bar.  Combat ensues.  Phylus has LIF 40, the dwarves both have LIF 25.  <br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Round 2!</strong>  <br>\\nFurbeard’s loyal (and very drunk) friend, Chief Burlap, rushes in to assist Furbeard in taking Phylus down.  Both dwarves attack.  Phylus tries to block the newcomer, Burlap, and then attack Furbeard to discourage the other dwarf from continuing this fight.<br>\\n<br>\\nPhylus rolls: <br>\\n(2d100) + dex (35) + Sword and Shield (40) + Wooden Shield (-1) =&gt; Might: 74, Roll: 23, 92<br>\\n(2d100) + str (40) + Sword and Shield (40) + Longsword (Medium) =&gt; Might: 80, Roll: 41, 99<br>\\n(2d100) + end (30) + Sword and Shield (40) + Wooden Shield (5) =&gt; Might: 75, Roll: 84, 2<br>\\n<br>\\nFurbeard rolls:<br>\\n(1d100) + dex (30) + Bar Combat (35) =&gt; Might: 65, Roll: 45<br>\\n(1d100) + str (50) + Bar Combat (35) + Metal Tankard (Light) =&gt; Might: 85, Roll: 43<br>\\n(1d100) + end (40) + Bar Combat (35) =&gt; Might: 75, Roll: 72<br>\\n<br>\\nChief Burlap rolls:<br>\\n(1d100) + dex (20) + Bar Combat (40) =&gt; Might: 60, Roll: 32<br>\\n(1d100) + str (60) + Bar Combat (40) + Pointy Tankard (Light) =&gt; Might: 100, Roll: 47<br>\\n(1d100) + end (30) + Bar Combat (40) =&gt; Might: 70, Roll: 17<br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Question 3</strong> - How much total damage does Furbeard take this round?\"\n  \'#description_display\': before\n  \'#type\': radios\n  \'#options\':\n    a1: 14-16\n    a2: 32-34\n    a3: 9-11\n    a4: \'\'\n  \'#options_randomize\': true\n  \'#required\': true\nquestion_12:\n  \'#title\': \"Case 4 - Combat\\nPhylus the nimble half-elf has ...\"\n  \'#description\': \"<strong>Case 4 - Combat</strong><br>\\nPhylus the nimble half-elf has run sour of a dwarf named Furbeard in a local bar.  Combat ensues.  Phylus has LIF 40, the dwarves both have LIF 25.  <br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Round 2!</strong>  <br>\\nFurbeard’s loyal (and very drunk) friend, Chief Burlap, rushes in to assist Furbeard in taking Phylus down.  Both dwarves attack.  Phylus tries to block the newcomer, Burlap, and then attack Furbeard to discourage the other dwarf from continuing this fight.<br>\\n<br>\\nPhylus rolls: <br>\\n(2d100) + dex (35) + Sword and Shield (40) + Wooden Shield (-1) =&gt; Might: 74, Roll: 23, 92<br>\\n(2d100) + str (40) + Sword and Shield (40) + Longsword (Medium) =&gt; Might: 80, Roll: 41, 99<br>\\n(2d100) + end (30) + Sword and Shield (40) + Wooden Shield (5) =&gt; Might: 75, Roll: 84, 2<br>\\n<br>\\nFurbeard rolls:<br>\\n(1d100) + dex (30) + Bar Combat (35) =&gt; Might: 65, Roll: 45<br>\\n(1d100) + str (50) + Bar Combat (35) + Metal Tankard (Light) =&gt; Might: 85, Roll: 43<br>\\n(1d100) + end (40) + Bar Combat (35) =&gt; Might: 75, Roll: 72<br>\\n<br>\\nChief Burlap rolls:<br>\\n(1d100) + dex (20) + Bar Combat (40) =&gt; Might: 60, Roll: 32<br>\\n(1d100) + str (60) + Bar Combat (40) + Pointy Tankard (Light) =&gt; Might: 100, Roll: 47<br>\\n(1d100) + end (30) + Bar Combat (40) =&gt; Might: 70, Roll: 17<br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Question 4</strong> - Given his Life score (25), what state is Furbeard now in?\"\n  \'#description_display\': before\n  \'#type\': radios\n  \'#options\':\n    a1: \'Still Fighting\'\n    a2: Unconscious\n    a3: Dead\n  \'#options_randomize\': true\n  \'#required\': true\nquestion_13:\n  \'#title\': \"Case 4 - Combat\\nPhylus the nimble half-elf has ...\"\n  \'#description\': \"<strong>Case 4 - Combat</strong><br>\\nPhylus the nimble half-elf has run sour of a dwarf named Furbeard in a local bar.  Combat ensues.  Phylus has LIF 40, the dwarves both have LIF 25.  <br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Round 3!</strong>  <br>\\nRealizing he’s hurt, Phylus tries a desperate maneuver.  Pointing his sword at Chief Burlap, he conjures the power of pure force and channels it directly at the dwarf’s chest, hoping to push him away and thus create a path of escape for himself.  Burlap, worried about just another sword chop like the one his partner got, attempts to block with his tankard.<br>\\n<br>\\nPhylus’ rolls:<br>\\n1d100 + int (40) + Telekinesis (50) =&gt; Might: 90, Roll: 62<br>\\n1d100 + spi (40) + Telekinesis (50) =&gt; Might: 90, Roll: 51<br>\\n<br>\\nChief Burlap’s rolls:<br>\\n(1d100) + dex (20) + Bar Combat (40) =&gt; Might: 60, Roll: 56<br>\\n(1d100) + str (60) + Bar Combat (40) + Pointy Tankard (Light) =&gt; Might: 100, Roll: 80<br>\\n(1d100) + end (30) + Bar Combat (40) =&gt; Might: 70, Roll: 42<br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Question 5</strong> - Did Phylus successfully cast the spell?  If so, did he affect Chief Burlap?<br>\\n<em>HINT: Remember that actively blocking changes the stats used to defend.  Account for that when ruling Phylus\' attack!</em>\"\n  \'#description_display\': before\n  \'#type\': radios\n  \'#options\':\n    a1: \'Neither, he failed to cast the spell.\'\n    a2: \'He cast the spell, but failed to affect Chief Burlap\'\n    a3: \'Both, he cast the spell and pushed Burlap back a bit\'\n  \'#options_randomize\': true\n  \'#required\': true\nquestion_14:\n  \'#title\': \"Case 4 - Combat\\nPhylus the nimble half-elf has ...\"\n  \'#description\': \"<strong>Case 4 - Combat</strong><br>\\nPhylus the nimble half-elf has run sour of a dwarf named Furbeard in a local bar.  Combat ensues.  Phylus has LIF 40, the dwarves both have LIF 25.  <br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Round 3!</strong>  <br>\\nRealizing he’s hurt, Phylus tries a desperate maneuver.  Pointing his sword at Chief Burlap, he conjures the power of pure force and channels it directly at the dwarf’s chest, hoping to push him away and thus create a path of escape for himself.  Burlap, worried about just another sword chop like the one his partner got, attempts to block with his tankard.<br>\\n<br>\\nPhylus’ rolls:<br>\\n1d100 + int (40) + Telekinesis (50) =&gt; Might: 90, Roll: 62<br>\\n1d100 + spi (40) + Telekinesis (50) =&gt; Might: 90, Roll: 51<br>\\n<br>\\nChief Burlap’s rolls:<br>\\n(1d100) + dex (20) + Bar Combat (40) =&gt; Might: 60, Roll: 56<br>\\n(1d100) + str (60) + Bar Combat (40) + Pointy Tankard (Light) =&gt; Might: 100, Roll: 80<br>\\n(1d100) + end (30) + Bar Combat (40) =&gt; Might: 70, Roll: 42<br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Question 6</strong> - How much did Burlap\'s block protect him?\"\n  \'#description_display\': before\n  \'#type\': radios\n  \'#options\':\n    a1: \"A bit: it subtracted 6 from Phylus\' 18 points produced\"\n    a2: \"A lot:  it subtracted 6 from Phylus\' 8 points produced\"\n    a3: \"Not much:  It subtracted 1 from Phylus\' 6 points produced\"\n    a4: \'Not at all:  Burlap failed to block the magical attack\'\n  \'#options_randomize\': true\n  \'#required\': true\nquestion_15:\n  \'#title\': \'Case 4 - Narrative\'\n  \'#description\': \"<strong>Case 4 - Combat</strong><br>\\nPhylus the nimble half-elf has run sour of a dwarf named Furbeard in a local bar.  Combat ensues.  Phylus has LIF 40, the dwarves both have LIF 25.  <br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Round 3!</strong>  <br>\\nRealizing he’s hurt, Phylus tries a desperate maneuver.  Pointing his sword at Chief Burlap, he conjures the power of pure force and channels it directly at the dwarf’s chest, hoping to push him away and thus create a path of escape for himself.  Burlap, worried about just another sword chop like the one his partner got, attempts to block with his tankard.<br>\\n<br>\\n<strong>Question 7</strong> - Assume Phylus succeeded with a net 15 points produced (after accounting for Furbeard’s block).  How would you determine how far back, in meters, Furbeard was pushed by the spell?\"\n  \'#description_display\': before\n  \'#type\': radios\n  \'#options\':\n    a1: \'Divide the PP by 7 and use yards or meters (about 2 meters, or 6 feet)\'\n    a2: \'Use the raw PP in yards or meters (15 meters, or about 50 feet)\'\n    a3: \'Use the raw PP, but in centimeters (15 centimeters, or half a foot)\'\n    a4: \'Just say \"he was pushed out of striking distance\"\'\n  \'#options_randomize\': true\n  \'#required\': true\nactions:\n  \'#submit__label\': Finish\n  \'#type\': webform_actions\n  \'#title\': \'Submit button(s)\'\n\";s:3:\"css\";s:0:\"\";s:10:\"javascript\";s:0:\"\";s:8:\"settings\";a:134:{s:4:\"ajax\";b:0;s:15:\"ajax_scroll_top\";s:4:\"form\";s:18:\"ajax_progress_type\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"ajax_effect\";s:0:\"\";s:10:\"ajax_speed\";N;s:4:\"page\";b:1;s:16:\"page_submit_path\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"page_confirm_path\";s:0:\"\";s:15:\"page_theme_name\";s:0:\"\";s:10:\"form_title\";s:4:\"both\";s:16:\"form_submit_once\";b:0;s:17:\"form_open_message\";s:0:\"\";s:18:\"form_close_message\";s:0:\"\";s:22:\"form_exception_message\";s:0:\"\";s:25:\"form_previous_submissions\";b:0;s:17:\"form_confidential\";b:0;s:25:\"form_confidential_message\";s:0:\"\";s:24:\"form_disable_remote_addr\";b:0;s:22:\"form_convert_anonymous\";b:0;s:16:\"form_prepopulate\";b:0;s:30:\"form_prepopulate_source_entity\";b:0;s:39:\"form_prepopulate_source_entity_required\";b:0;s:35:\"form_prepopulate_source_entity_type\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"form_unsaved\";b:0;s:17:\"form_disable_back\